semantic_diff: >-
  Base: revision 2, digest
  sha256:9008a22eb8fee98028e3447a8b19ab5855db63cac0805707e43869a772e0d5e4.
  Stage 2 orchestrated mining
  (planning-records/ammo/stage2-orchestrated-mining.md), flat in this graph.
  Counts: 13 nodes become 15, 47 edges become 50, 31 checks become 34, 13
  roles become 15, 16 evidence definitions become 18, 45 outcomes become 47,
  5 control nodes become 6. 1369 lines become 1529 (190 added, 30 removed,
  13 hunks). No package test pins graph size.
  (1) The gap. One researcher holds the global trace read and five
  independent source, roofline, and library investigations in one context,
  and the first independent check of any of it is the stage audit. A family
  investigation is local work. It can run in parallel and be reviewed alone
  before the report uses it. The tables and the report are global work and
  stay with one researcher each (§9.12: the parts can run in parallel, and
  an intermediate result needs its own review). This holds for any target
  with more than one hot kernel family. It does not depend on one run.
  (2) The shape. stage_2_bottleneck_mining now mines the tables only
  (ammo_researcher, task_type mining_tables) and ends tables_ready.
  tables_to_dossiers fans out family_dossier over selected_families under
  mined_json_valid: family_worker at pave-init:orchestrate-worker and
  family_reviewer at pave-init:adversarial-investigator, one wave, four
  review rounds at most. Each run ends grounded or ungrounded and joins
  all_dossiers_terminal, which resumes at synthesize_report
  (ammo_researcher, task_type mining_report). report_written reaches
  audit_s2 by the live edge mining_to_audit_s2, which now leaves the new
  node. bottleneck_analysis keeps its name, artifact, and consumers; only
  its producer moves to synthesize_report. Outcomes mining_grounded and
  mining_incomplete go; tables_ready, grounded, ungrounded, and
  report_written come in. user_authority_needed and its pause edge stay,
  and its meaning now names the case the smoke ended in (item 12).
  (3) The audit stays, at the same strength. audit_s2 keeps its auditor,
  audit_gate block, stamps, verdict file, outcome tokens, three-cycle cap
  (audit_cycle_bound), delegate, and investigator. Its consumes gain
  mined_tables and family_dossier, so its scope covers the tables and the
  dossiers. Its blocked meaning no longer names one owner, because two
  edges now route the repair by the cited file (item 5). audit_nodes,
  outcome_tokens, audit_s2_passed, and the audit_s2 pass, investigate, and
  escalation edges are unchanged.
  (4) The enrichment order is unchanged. mining_enrichment_recorded keeps
  its question and still guards mining_to_audit_s2, so enrich --mining (or
  serving-sync for a serving target) lands before every audit cycle, as
  SKILL.md Stage 2 says today. scripts/ammo_state.py names T_AUDIT_S2 as
  the next step only after bottleneck_mining.completed_at exists (1967 to
  1988). The check's on_failure_route moves to synthesize_report, the node
  that now writes the report. The design draft moved the check after the
  audit, which would have flipped that order.
  (5) Audit repair goes to the owner of the cited file, upstream first.
  audit_s2_blocked_to_mining gains blocker_in_tables (a BLOCKING or HIGH
  finding cites a file outside mining/families/ and the report), and the
  new tables fan out every family again. The new
  audit_s2_blocked_to_dossiers fans out over audit_repair_families under
  blocker_in_dossiers_or_report (findings cite only those files). That
  reopens only the cited families. With none cited it opens no run, the
  barrier holds, and the report is written again. This is the live S45
  pattern (audit_s45_blocked_to_track_repair, audit_repair_tracks). The two
  checks are exclusive and exhaustive, as pave-yaml.md §12.3 requires: a
  finding that cites no file fails the first and passes the second, so the
  report is written again.
  (6) Selection floor and cap (open question 1). The selected_families
  field states the rule and points at scripts/mine_trace.py, which states
  the two reasons given here. A family is selected when its highest f_e2e
  across buckets reaches campaign.config.min_e2e_improvement_pct, read as a
  share. Families are ranked by that value and at most five are kept. A
  family below the campaign floor cannot yield a gain at that floor on its
  own. Five families plus the cross_cutting entry make six workers, which
  is the orchestrate wave cap (skills/orchestrate/SKILL.md, Cap a wave at 6
  workers). So the wave is always one wave. A family the cap drops stays
  in tables.md. mined_json_valid checks the cap and that the fan-out
  collection equals the selection plus cross_cutting. It absorbs the
  draft's families_match_selection check. scripts/mine_trace.py implements
  the rule.
  (7) Codex (open question 2). The design record says the orchestrate
  skill is Claude Code only. That is stale: pave-init 2.8.3 ships
  codex/skills/orchestrate, and it needs Codex V2 agent tools
  (codex/README.md, Orchestrate). Claude Code and Codex V2 run the wave
  through the orchestrate skill. Codex V1 (Bedrock) cannot. The
  family_worker and family_reviewer purposes say that
  references/harness-binding.md binds a one-shot seat where the skill
  cannot run, with the same outcomes and the same round bound. The graph
  keeps one meaning on every harness, because seats are run setup (§2.1)
  and harness-binding.md is the one AMMO file that chooses a harness.
  (8) Serving targets run the same nodes. stage_2_bottleneck_mining writes
  the mining record that references/serving-campaign.md defines, and
  mined_json_valid checks it with an empty collection. The fan-out opens
  no run, the barrier holds at once, and the report and the audit run as
  for a batch target.
  (9) Cuts against the design record and its draft (§4.11: prefer the
  existing gate, and remove any element whose absence changes nothing).
  The tables-only reviewer brief goes, and so does a partition_wrong
  outcome with its route. T_AUDIT_S2's BLOCKING partition bullet checks
  the same claim before the same harm, and the audit routes it to the
  tables under the cycle counter that state.json already persists. A
  worker who finds its family's patterns or ceiling wrong ends its dossier
  UNGROUNDED with the evidence. The report_tables_verbatim check goes,
  because the audit's BLOCKING bullet on hand-edited tables covers it. The
  input_defect and report_incomplete outcomes go, and so does the live
  mining_retry self-loop: the checks' on_failure_route carries a
  lead-detected retry, as mining_enrichment_recorded already did. Three
  blocked edges and three owner checks become two of each. The draft's
  lead writing UNGROUNDED into a dossier goes: the lead role now forbids a
  mining artifact write, so the worker writes the last line. Revision 2's
  names replace stale draft names: adversarial_investigator for
  ammo_investigator, blocker_record for mining_blocker, and
  user_authority_needed for authority_needed. The draft's added sentences
  in audit_s2_passed and audit_verdict go.
  (10) The composed shape is replaced (§9.12.1, §4.11). The first draft of
  this revision put Stage 2 in a child graph file with the audit inside
  it. §9.12.1 keeps a decomposition in one graph unless the subgraph is
  reused, owned or delivered separately, or too large to review. None
  holds for Stage 2. §4.11 prefers the existing gate, and audit_s2 already
  is that gate. The composed form grew the bundle by 365 lines (the parent
  at 1342 plus a 392-line child) and moved audit_s2 and its tokens into the
  child. The flat form grows it by 160 lines, 205 fewer, and keeps
  audit_s2 where it is. The child's terminals, inputs, exports, the
  composition block, and the moved audit tokens are gone with it.
  (11) Cost per run. Today a Stage 2 pass costs one researcher plus one
  auditor per audit cycle. On Claude Code a pass now costs: one researcher
  for the tables; up to six orchestrate workers (opus) and two reviewers
  (fable), with one to four review rounds per dossier and the orchestrate
  whole-goal review round; one researcher for the report (the miner may be
  resumed); and one auditor per cycle. That is up to eight added seats per
  pass when the miner is resumed for the report, and nine when it is not.
  On Codex V1 (references/harness-binding.md § Stage 2 Family Wave) every
  round is a fresh one-shot researcher and a fresh reviewer, so six
  families at four rounds is up to 48 dispatches in the worst case; the
  user approved the cost as priced for Claude Code. A serving pass adds
  one researcher dispatch or resume. An upstream
  audit blocker reruns the whole wave. A dossier blocker reruns only the
  cited families. Stage 2 runs in round 1, after every material SHIP, and
  after invalidated mining. The lead adds two mechanical checks per pass
  and two per blocked cycle. No run has measured the wave's wall clock or
  its effect on audit cycles.
  (12) Usage evidence. No usage log exists: plan.md records neither
  approval nor usage_log, so approval is treated as always. The only
  predecessor run is the g6e-cdd smoke. It was unpinned, ran Stage 1 and a
  Stage 2 mine_trace dry run, and is paused. It changed two things here.
  First, the principle that scripts/mine_trace.py cuts every per-bucket
  slice and no slice is cut by hand: in the smoke one researcher cut the
  slices by hand, recut them, and wrote its own slicer (smoke-g6e-cdd.md
  290, 295, 442, 498; prompt-audit/stage-2.md row 9; adoption.md R17).
  Second, user_authority_needed names the case the smoke ended in: a
  script FATAL from a toolkit defect that no input or config change fixes
  (smoke-g6e-cdd.md 7, 25). The round default (row 6) is a script change
  with no graph change. The smoke never reached the family wave, the
  report, or T_AUDIT_S2, so nothing in the wave is field-tested.
  plan_evidence is provisional for that reason.
  (13) User-only check (revision rule 6): approved by the user on
  2026-10-29 for the budget (the approval field quotes it); the lead
  records the apply step's own approval at apply. Budgets: touched, since
  a pass adds up to eight or nine seats and one to four review rounds per
  dossier (item 11). Effects: touched, two forbidden effects added, both
  tighter. The lead role may no longer write a mining artifact, a family
  dossier included (the hunk at line 83), and the new family_worker role
  may edit only its own dossier. No effect that was forbidden is now
  allowed. Check strength: unchanged. audit_s2 is the same gate with the
  same cap, and its scope widens. The new checks only add, and the live
  mining_incomplete self-report becomes a lead check route. requirements.md
  decision 4 (graph faithfulness): the 7 stages and 4 audits hold,
  stage_nodes still names one node per stage, and nothing is removed.
  Stage 2 now spans three nodes; the user reads that with the budget
  change. Root goal, external access, interfaces, and state authority:
  unchanged. Mining files stay under the round's mining/
  folder. state.json stays the only run state. The plugin already depends
  on pave-init for the adversarial investigator, and the orchestrate skill
  and its worker come from the same plugin. Stage 3 reads the same
  bottleneck_analysis.md.
  (14) Old wording, searched across the package outside history/ and
  revisions.yaml: no survivor. The graph names none of the removed
  outcomes or edges. The companion files no longer name the child run,
  the child graph file, or a parent outcome, and
  tests/test_guidance_semantic_contract.py guards that. The README § 8
  diagram already draws the flat shape; only its validator count line
  waits for apply. On a scratch copy with this diff applied,
  tests/test_workflow_pave.py passes 18 and fails 4, all pins:
  EXPECTED_COUNTS, EXPECTED_NODES, EXPECTED_CONTROL_NODES, and the README
  and VERSION counts. They are re-pinned after apply.
  tests/test_codex_port.py fails its two verify tests only because a
  hand-applied scratch has no revision entry.
  tests/test_preflight_pumice_host.py fails one test with or without this
  diff. The audit_s2 keyword in scripts/ammo_state.py (1362, 1545, 1988)
  is the audit.stage_2 stamp key and this node's name, so it stays.
