changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 3: Stage 2 mines in three steps. One researcher mines the
  tables. One worker per selected kernel family writes a reviewed dossier,
  all in one wave. The researcher then writes the report, and T_AUDIT_S2
  judges the report, the tables, and the dossiers at the same gate as
  before. A family is selected when its highest end-to-end share reaches
  the campaign floor, five at most. An audit finding reopens the tables,
  or only the families it cites. Landing alongside: scripts/mine_trace.py
  (selection, family chains, the round default, the slicer) and
  scripts/artifact_layout.json (the mining/families/ slot) with their
  tests; skills/ammo/SKILL.md Stage 2; agents/ammo-researcher.md task
  types mining_tables, mining_report, and mining_dossier; the new
  orchestration/mining-orchestration.md and references/mining-dossier.md;
  the audit-invariants bullet; the audit-protocol row and the other
  T_AUDIT_S2 mentions; the ammo_state.py Stage 2 next-step text;
  references/harness-binding.md for the Codex binding; the Codex port; the
  spawn guard. After apply, the test counts and the README and VERSION
  counts are re-pinned.
